! Written disabled, matching nothing:
!   firewall 1 (Never to the blocklist (floating)): zones WAN, DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 2 (Never to the blocklist (floating) 2): references 'Geo_block': an alias of type 'geoip' (the countries of a GeoIP database), whose addresses are not in the configuration; zones WAN, DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 3 (Guests never to the blocklist): not converted: it matches the source of traffic that leaves, which is the source after outbound NAT; zones WAN: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 4 (DMZ may not send mail out (received-on)): zones DMZ, WAN: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 5 (Voice from the partner - pass): zones WAN: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 6 (Block private networks from WAN): zones WAN: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 7 (VPN users to the web servers): zones OpenVPN, VPNSITE: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 8 (No outside resolver (group)): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 9 (Inside may ping (old kind)): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2); an ICMP type or code: a policy matches every ICMP message or none
!   firewall 11 (Web publishing): zones WAN: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 12 (DMZ anywhere but LAN (disabled)): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 13 (DMZ ICMPv6): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2); no service the router's IPv4 policies can match
!   firewall 14 (Servers fetch updates): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2); 'Updates' holds members only its platform knows
!   firewall 15 (Servers fetch updates 2): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 16 (Servers fetch updates 3): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2); 'Updates' holds members only its platform knows
!   firewall 17 (Servers fetch updates 4): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 18 (Guests stay out): zones GUEST: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 19 (Guests to the portal (no protocol, both IP versions)): zones GUEST: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 20 (DMZ anywhere but LAN (disabled) 2): zones DMZ: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 21 (Guests interactive (tos)): not converted: it matches the type of service (tos) '0x10'; zones GUEST: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 22 (VPN users to LAN web (old kind)): zones OpenVPN, VPNSITE: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
